Package: cursor-spend-monitor
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-gi, gir1.2-notify-0.7, libnotify-bin, gnome-shell
Maintainer: Fredrick Makoffu <fredrickmakoffu@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/fredrickmakoffu/cursor-spend-monitor
Description: AI coding usage limits in the GNOME top bar
 A daemon that tracks usage limits for AI coding tools (Cursor, Claude Code,
 OpenCode) and a GNOME Shell extension that shows them as a status dot in the
 top bar. Log out and back in after installing so GNOME Shell loads the
 extension, then run `cursor-spend-monitor setup`.
